E-01 server 120.79.148.0:8443  aneb-server/0.1.0
Run date: 2026-07-12 (UTC)  Operator: automated (c11)
Acceptance: per-group P95 |pcap_ts - event_wall| < 2ms ; crosspkt/parse-fail < 5%
====================================================================

METHOD
------
- Capture on server, bounded filter 'tcp port 8443 and src port 8443',
  src port 8443 only (server->client direction):
    tcpdump -i any -tt -A -l -s 0 'tcp port 8443 and src port 8443'
  Link type: LINUX_SLL2 (Linux cooked v2, from -i any). Text mode (-tt -A),
  no binary pcap parsing. Capture bounded (manual stop right after stream),
  temp files in /tmp, deleted after analysis. aneb-server systemd unit
  untouched (never restarted); no other service touched.
- Client load generated from Windows host, DIRECT (proxy bypassed):
    curl.exe --noproxy '*' -sN <url>
  (system proxy 127.0.0.1:33210/7897 bypassed per D-16; measuring RTT/timestamps
   through the proxy would inflate them ~54x.)
- Event wall-clock mapping (per analyzer /tmp/c11_analyze.py):
    event_wall_ns = anchor_wall_unix_ns + pre_flush_us * 1000
  KEY FINDING on the mapping: anchor_wall_unix_ns is a CONSTANT across every
  request (1783843344665294456 in both groups, and identical in a probe hours
  earlier) = the process-start wall-clock. pre_flush_us (and the prelude's
  srv_ts_us) are MONOTONIC microseconds SINCE process start, so pre_flush_us is
  added directly to the anchor -- do NOT subtract srv_ts_us. Verified on
  uniform seq0: anchor/1000 + pre_flush_us = 1783866384901447 us vs pcap
  1783866384.901453 -> 6 us. This matches the task's stated formula
  (anchor + pre_flush*1000); srv_ts_us is only the prelude's own monotonic
  stamp, not part of the mapping.
- diff_us = pcap_packet_ts_us - event_wall_us. Reported |diff| percentiles.
- One data-event per packet (each event flushed individually). Events whose
  'data:{"seq"...}' opens in a packet but whose JSON does not close in that same
  packet are counted as cross-packet and dropped. Duplicate seqs (TCP
  retransmit / any-iface double capture) deduped keeping earliest packet ts.

