VERDICT:  PASS (both groups)
  uniform P95=79.9 us , burst P95=61.9 us  (budget 2000 us)
  cross-packet / parse-fail ratio = 0.00% both groups (budget <5%)

Caveat on the anchor mapping bias (as required):
  event_wall is derived from a one-shot process-start wall<->monotonic anchor
  (anchor_wall_unix_ns). Any systematic offset in that single anchor mapping
  shifts ALL events by the same constant, so it lands in the SIGNED mean
  (uniform +83 us, burst +45 us) but does not widen the per-event spread that
  P95 |diff| measures. chrony holds the E-01 system clock to ~86 us RMS, so the
  anchor's contribution is at the ~0.1 ms level -- negligible vs the 2 ms budget
  and consistent with the small positive signed bias observed.

